research/_codex/P13-codex-r1.log:1610:For suite choice, distinguish **full autonomy research** from **cost-realistic Indian ADAS**. Waymo states its sixth-generation system uses **13 cameras, four lidars and six radars**. [Waymo](https://waymo.com/blog/2024/08/meet-the-6th-generation-waymo-driver/). Tesla documents camera-based Tesla Vision for specified Model 3/Y markets; it also states currently enabled Autopilot/FSD features do **not** make those vehicles autonomous. [Tesla](https://www.tesla.com/en_gb/support/autopilot). India-facing examples differ: [Minus Zero](https://minuszero.ai/technology) describes a camera-input approach, while Mahindra’s [XUV 3XO](https://auto.mahindra.com/press-release/mahindra-launches-the-xuv-3xo-a-disruptor-in-compact-suvs.html) advertises one radar plus one vision camera for Level 2 ADAS. Swaayatt’s [public technology page](https://www.swaayattrobots.com/) does not specify a complete current sensor bill; **UNVERIFIED**. For your *simulation research*, I would test a camera+radar production-style suite **and** a camera+radar+lidar diagnostic suite. Cost figures require a separate, current parts quotation.
